<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aulus Vibenna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aulus Vibenna (Etruscan Avle Vipinas) was an Etruscan warrior of the 6th century BCE from Vulci, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caelius-vibenna">Caelius Vibenna</a>. He appears in the paintings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-tomb">François Tomb</a>, and a bucchero vessel dedicated in his name at Veii suggests he was a historical figure. Roman tradition linked his name to the legend of the head found on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitol</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aulus-vibenna.jpg" alt="Aulus Vibenna" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlo Ruspi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fran%C3%A7ois_Tomb_Carlo_Ruspi_08.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
